## Style guides and standards cited in the presets

The preset files cite external style guides and standards per rule (Google,
Microsoft, Apple, IBM, GOV.UK, GitLab, plainlanguage.gov, Chicago, Duden,
DIN 5008, DIN SPEC 33429, Hohenheimer Verständlichkeitsindex). These are cited
as sources for the substance of a rule. No text from them is reproduced here,
and no claim is made to any right in them. Each bracket code in a preset file
resolves to a URL in that file's Sources block.

## German-language projects consulted

The German preset's Sources block credits several German AI-writing projects,
chiefly `marmbiz/humanizer-de` (MIT), `severinschweiger/klartext`, and
`LangeVC/txtHumanizer` (Apache-2.0). They were consulted as sources for which
patterns matter in German and for process-level lessons, recorded in the
preset's "Lessons beyond pattern content" section. Rule text in this repository
is written for this project; no rule text, example, or code was copied from
them. Note that pattern-catalog material in `marmbiz/humanizer-de` is itself
CC BY-SA 4.0 per that project's NOTICE, so any future verbatim reuse of its
examples would carry that license rather than MIT.

All other project code and original material are licensed under the MIT License
unless a file contains a more specific notice.
